{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1502819294,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNTAzODY1NTA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1718","origin":"github"},"title":"--annonimize-date ","message":"git annex now allows to specify the date for to be used while recording time stamp(s) within git-annex branch files.  It allows now to fake all the dates stored in the git/git-annex repo:\n\n```shell\n$\u003e da=40; d0=\"Thu Jan 1 00:00:$da 1970 +0000\"; rm -rf /tmp/test; GIT_ANNEX_VECTOR_CLOCK=$da GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=\"$d0\" GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=\"$d0\" datalad create /tmp/test\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/test\ncreate(ok): /tmp/test (dataset)                                                                                                                         \n2 10381.....................................:Tue 15 Aug 2017 01:33:12 PM EDT:.\nhopa:/tmp\n$\u003e git -C /tmp/test log -p git-annex\ncommit 5af2c2a04319a362417250aef269002e25c1d356 (git-annex)\nAuthor: Yaroslav Halchenko \u003cdebian@onerussian.com\u003e\nDate:   Thu Jan 1 00:00:40 1970 +0000\n\n    update\n\ndiff --git a/uuid.log b/uuid.log\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..748db51\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/uuid.log\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+97b0f01c-d7eb-44ed-813f-7c0723fd8a90 yoh@hopa:/tmp/test timestamp=40s\n\ncommit 0096b601c565ac1efd2535363880ebe7c8f278e1\nAuthor: Yaroslav Halchenko \u003cdebian@onerussian.com\u003e\nDate:   Thu Jan 1 00:00:40 1970 +0000\n```\n\nWe are going to use it within the scope of heudiconv, but I wondered if we should provide interface to this functionality within datalad itself.\n\n- pros: might come handy in other use cases where dates should be obfuscated\n- cons: REALLY easy to shot yourself in the foot, so it would warrant at least some checks (that previous commit in git and git-annex has date(s) before or == etc)","files":null}]}